BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Fiery Caldera to Hidden Gem: A Short History of Sugarloaf Rid
 ge State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T110000
UID:47341b22c6c5f2cafba9e328eeab7fbc@visitsantarosa.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Sugarloaf docents to learn about the history of Sugarloaf
  Ridge State Park—from its volcanic beginnings 3-5 million years ago\, t
 hrough the indigenous Wappo who tended its forests\, fields and streams fo
 r over 10\,000 years from their village of Wilikos at the headwaters of So
 noma Creek\, to homestead settlements and their ingenious adaptations to o
 ur isolation and serpentine soils. We will also touch on the park’s natu
 ral history which intersects its human history in often interesting ways. 
 Me
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Road\, Kenwood\, C
 A 95452
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/from-fiery-caldera-to-hidden-gem
 -a-short-history-of-sugarloaf-ridge-state-park/
X-SOURCE:Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
